<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <!--
    Customer Portal web-app demo on ASP.NET Core (mirror of demos\60.HTML\04.Portal).

    The 60.HTML version hosts a TsgcWebSocketHTTPServer and renders every page in
    DispatchRequest. This mirror keeps the SAME reusable logic (sgcPortal_Bcrypt.cs,
    sgcPortal_Config.cs, sgcPortal_DB.cs, sgcPortal_I18n.cs, sgcPortal_Pages.cs,
    sgcPortal_Passkeys.cs, sgcPortal_Sessions.cs and sgcPortal_Types.cs are copied
    VERBATIM) but hosts it on Kestrel: the ASP.NET Core adapter serves the built-in
    client assets (Bootstrap / Chart.js / htmx, all by file name) and the htmx
    WebSocket channel, and this app owns every page route via Minimal API
    endpoints. Auth (bcrypt + WebAuthn passkeys), the in-memory cookie session
    store, i18n and the SQLite CRUD are all the reused plain-C# files; only the
    hosting layer (Program.cs + sgcPortalWebHost.cs) is new.

    This mirrors the host pattern established by the 01.ERP / 02.AdminCRUD ports.
    The Portal-specific part is the DUAL-AREA role model: a role 'customer' login
    is confined to its self-service area (orders / profile / support), while an
    'admin' or 'user' login reaches the back-office (customers / providers /
    products / invoices / reports), with 'admin' additionally owning users +
    settings + firewall + audit. See sgcPortalWebHost.Guarded / GuardedStaff /
    GuardedAdmin / GuardedCustomer + RootGet.

    The two host files that were NOT copied are sgcPortal_Server.cs (the
    TsgcWebSocketHTTPServer host) and the console Program.cs.

    Nullable + ImplicitUsings are disabled: the reused files carry no nullable
    reference annotations (they predate them), matching the 60.HTML build.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Portal</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>sgcPortalWeb</AssemblyName>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\src\sgcHTML.AspNetCore\esegece.sgcHTML.AspNetCore.csproj" Condition="'$(SgcHTMLAspNetCoreUseProject)' == 'true'" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Same SQLite provider + version the 60.HTML console demo used. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.Sqlite" Version="8.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Update="sgcPortalServer.conf.json">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
